---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/sections/PageHero.astro";
import LegalContent from "../components/sections/LegalContent.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — WAYGGO Charters"
  description="How WAYGGO Charters collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information when you use our website and group transportation services."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy-policy" }]}
>
  <PageHero
    badge="Our Policies"
    heading="Privacy Policy"
    subheading="Your Information. Our Responsibility."
    size="sm"
  />

  <LegalContent>
    <p>At WAYGGO Charters, transportation is built around relationships.</p>
    <p>We work with customers, travel professionals, tour operators, travel agencies, transportation partners, operators, travelers, employees, website visitors, and other people who help make group travel possible.</p>
    <p>Those relationships often require us to handle information.</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how WAYGGO Charters (“WAYGGO,” “we,” “our,” or “us”) collects, uses, shares, protects, and otherwise handles personal information when you interact with our website, communicate with us, request transportation services, work with us as a partner, or otherwise engage with WAYGGO.</p>
    <p>Our goal is straightforward:</p>
    <p><strong>To handle information responsibly, use it for legitimate business purposes, and communicate clearly about what we do with it.</strong></p>

    <h2>Who This Policy Applies To</h2>
    <p>This Privacy Policy applies to personal information we may collect from or about:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Website visitors</li>
      <li>Customers and prospective customers</li>
      <li>International tour operators</li>
      <li>Travel agencies and travel professionals</li>
      <li>Corporate and event planners</li>
      <li>Wedding and special-event organizers</li>
      <li>Educational and student-tour organizers</li>
      <li>Religious and pilgrimage group organizers</li>
      <li>Sports teams and fan-group organizers</li>
      <li>Transportation partners and local operators</li>
      <li>Drivers or transportation personnel where applicable</li>
      <li>Travelers and passengers</li>
      <li>Business contacts and representatives</li>
      <li>People who communicate with WAYGGO</li>
      <li>Other individuals whose information is provided to us in connection with transportation services</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Not every section will apply to every person.</p>
    <p>For example, a website visitor may provide information through a contact form, while a transportation partner may provide business, compliance, insurance, and operational information as part of the partner relationship.</p>

    <h2>Information We May Collect</h2>
    <p>The information we collect depends on how you interact with WAYGGO and the services involved.</p>
    <h3>Information You Provide Directly</h3>
    <p>You may provide information when you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request a quote</li>
      <li>Submit a transportation inquiry</li>
      <li>Register as a partner</li>
      <li>Contact our team</li>
      <li>Communicate about an existing booking</li>
      <li>Provide itinerary information</li>
      <li>Enter information into a website form</li>
      <li>Communicate by email, telephone, or other channels</li>
      <li>Participate in a business relationship with WAYGGO</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This information may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>Company or organization</li>
      <li>Job title or role</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Telephone number</li>
      <li>Business address</li>
      <li>Billing or invoicing information</li>
      <li>Travel dates</li>
      <li>Group size</li>
      <li>Pickup and destination information</li>
      <li>Itinerary details</li>
      <li>Vehicle requirements</li>
      <li>Special transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Other information you choose to provide</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information About Travelers and Groups</h2>
    <p>When WAYGGO helps coordinate group transportation, information about travelers may sometimes be provided to us by a customer, travel professional, tour operator, event organizer, school, religious organization, sports organization, or another party arranging transportation.</p>
    <p>Depending on the service, this information may include details necessary to coordinate the journey, such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Passenger names</li>
      <li>Group or booking identifiers</li>
      <li>Pickup and drop-off information</li>
      <li>Travel or itinerary information</li>
      <li>Accessibility or mobility requirements</li>
      <li>Luggage or equipment requirements</li>
      <li>Other transportation-related requirements</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you provide personal information about another person to WAYGGO, you should have the appropriate authority or permission to provide that information where required by applicable law.</p>
    <p>Where possible, we encourage organizations arranging group transportation to provide only the information necessary for the transportation service.</p>

    <h2>Information We Collect Automatically</h2>
    <p>When you visit our website or interact with our digital services, certain information may be collected automatically.</p>
    <p>Depending on how the website and its technologies are configured, this may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address</li>
      <li>Browser type</li>
      <li>Device type</li>
      <li>Operating system</li>
      <li>Pages visited</li>
      <li>Referring pages</li>
      <li>Approximate location derived from technical information</li>
      <li>Date and time of visits</li>
      <li>Website interaction information</li>
      <li>Technical and diagnostic information</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This information may help us understand how the website is used, maintain website functionality, improve performance, protect our systems, and understand how people discover and interact with WAYGGO.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may use cookies and similar technologies to support website functionality, remember preferences, understand website usage, improve the user experience, and support other legitimate website purposes.</p>
    <p>The technologies used may vary as our website and digital services evolve.</p>
    <p>Where required by applicable law, we will provide appropriate choices or notices concerning certain cookies or similar technologies.</p>
    <p>You may also be able to manage cookies through your browser or device settings.</p>
    <p>Disabling certain cookies may affect how parts of the website function.</p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We use personal information for purposes connected to our business, our relationships, and the transportation services we provide.</p>
    <p>These purposes may include:</p>
    <h4>Providing Transportation Services</h4>
    <p>To respond to inquiries, prepare quotes, coordinate transportation, manage bookings, communicate itinerary information, and support group journeys.</p>
    <h4>Coordinating With Transportation Partners</h4>
    <p>To share information with appropriate transportation operators and service providers when necessary to arrange and operate transportation.</p>
    <h4>Managing Business Relationships</h4>
    <p>To communicate with customers, travel professionals, partners, suppliers, and other business contacts.</p>
    <h4>Supporting Operations</h4>
    <p>To coordinate scheduling, dispatch, billing, invoicing, customer service, quality processes, and other business operations.</p>
    <h4>Improving Our Services</h4>
    <p>To understand how our services and website are being used and identify opportunities to improve the WAYGGO experience.</p>
    <h4>Maintaining Safety and Quality</h4>
    <p>To support appropriate transportation, operational, compliance, and quality-assurance processes.</p>
    <h4>Protecting Our Business and Users</h4>
    <p>To detect, investigate, prevent, or address fraud, misuse, security incidents, unauthorized activity, disputes, or other risks.</p>
    <h4>Meeting Legal Obligations</h4>
    <p>To comply with applicable laws, regulations, legal processes, and legitimate governmental requests.</p>
    <h4>Communicating With You</h4>
    <p>To respond to questions, provide service-related information, and, where permitted, send relevant business communications.</p>

    <h2>How WAYGGO Works With Transportation Partners</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO operates through a transportation network that may involve independent transportation companies and other service providers.</p>
    <p>When transportation is being arranged, information necessary to perform the service may be shared with the appropriate transportation partner.</p>
    <p>For example, a transportation operator may need information about:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pickup and drop-off locations</li>
      <li>Date and time</li>
      <li>Group size</li>
      <li>Passenger or group requirements</li>
      <li>Luggage or equipment</li>
      <li>Special transportation requirements</li>
      <li>Relevant itinerary details</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The purpose of sharing this information is to coordinate and provide the transportation service.</p>
    <p>WAYGGO does not treat the information provided for a transportation booking as an invitation for unrelated use.</p>

    <h2>Information Provided to WAYGGO by Customers and Partners</h2>
    <p>Customers and business partners may provide WAYGGO with information about other people as part of an itinerary or business relationship.</p>
    <p>For example, a tour operator may provide passenger or itinerary information in order to arrange transportation.</p>
    <p>In these situations, the organization providing the information may have its own responsibilities under applicable privacy laws.</p>
    <p>We encourage customers and partners to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide only information reasonably necessary for the service</li>
      <li>Avoid providing unnecessary sensitive information</li>
      <li>Inform travelers when their information needs to be shared for transportation purposes</li>
      <li>Handle information responsibly before providing it to WAYGGO</li>
    </ul>
    <p>WAYGGO will use information received in connection with transportation for appropriate business and service purposes.</p>

    <h2>Information Sharing</h2>
    <p>We may share personal information with appropriate parties when reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.</p>
    <p>These parties may include:</p>
    <h4>Transportation Operators</h4>
    <p>Local transportation companies and operators responsible for providing transportation.</p>
    <h4>Service Providers</h4>
    <p>Companies that help us operate our website, communications, technology, payment processes, business systems, or other business functions.</p>
    <h4>Customers and Business Partners</h4>
    <p>Where necessary to coordinate transportation or fulfill the services requested.</p>
    <h4>Professional Advisors</h4>
    <p>Professional service providers such as legal, accounting, insurance, or other advisors where appropriate.</p>
    <h4>Government and Regulatory Authorities</h4>
    <p>Where required or permitted by applicable law.</p>
    <h4>Business Transactions</h4>
    <p>Where information may be transferred as part of a merger, acquisition, financing, restructuring, sale of assets, or similar business transaction, subject to applicable law.</p>
    <p>We do not share personal information simply because it is available to us.</p>
    <p>We consider the purpose for which the information was collected and the role of the party receiving it.</p>

    <h2>Selling Personal Information</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO does not intend to sell personal information in the ordinary course of providing group transportation services.</p>
    <p>If our practices change in a way that requires additional notice or choices under applicable privacy law, we will provide those notices and choices as required.</p>

    <h2>Marketing Communications</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may communicate with customers, prospective customers, partners, and business contacts about services, company information, transportation solutions, or other relevant business matters.</p>
    <p>Where required, marketing communications will provide an appropriate way to unsubscribe or manage communication preferences.</p>
    <p>Even if you opt out of marketing communications, we may still send service-related or transactional communications when necessary.</p>

    <h2>Business-to-Business Information</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO works extensively with businesses and professional organizations.</p>
    <p>Information relating to a business contact may include professional information such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>Job title</li>
      <li>Company</li>
      <li>Business email</li>
      <li>Business telephone number</li>
      <li>Business address</li>
      <li>Professional communications</li>
      <li>Account or partnership information</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We use this information to maintain legitimate business relationships, communicate about services, coordinate transportation, and manage our operations.</p>
    <p>Where applicable privacy laws protect business-contact information as personal information, we handle it accordingly.</p>

    <h2>Transportation Partner Information</h2>
    <p>Transportation partners may provide information to WAYGGO as part of the partner relationship.</p>
    <p>Depending on the relationship and applicable requirements, this may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Business contact information</li>
      <li>Company information</li>
      <li>Licensing information</li>
      <li>Insurance information</li>
      <li>Vehicle information</li>
      <li>Compliance documentation</li>
      <li>Operational information</li>
      <li>Driver-related information where appropriate and permitted</li>
      <li>Quality and performance information</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This information may be used to evaluate, manage, coordinate, and support transportation partnerships and network operations.</p>
    <p>Partner information is treated as business information entrusted to WAYGGO and is handled according to the purpose for which it was provided and applicable legal requirements.</p>

    <h2>Sensitive Information</h2>
    <p>Some transportation situations may involve information that is more sensitive than ordinary business or contact information.</p>
    <p>For example, a traveler or group may communicate an accessibility, mobility, dietary, medical, or other requirement relevant to the transportation service.</p>
    <p>We encourage customers and partners to provide only information that is reasonably necessary to arrange the service.</p>
    <p>Where sensitive information is necessary, WAYGGO will handle it in accordance with applicable law and for the relevant service or business purpose.</p>
    <p>We do not ask customers to provide sensitive information simply because it may be interesting or useful.</p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO retains information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, including providing services, maintaining business and financial records, resolving disputes, protecting our interests, meeting legal obligations, and supporting legitimate business operations.</p>
    <p>The appropriate retention period can vary depending on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The type of information</li>
      <li>The nature of the relationship</li>
      <li>The service involved</li>
      <li>Legal or regulatory requirements</li>
      <li>Accounting or business requirements</li>
      <li>Whether a dispute or legal matter exists</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not retain personal information indefinitely simply because we can.</p>
    <p>When information is no longer reasonably required, it may be deleted, anonymized, or otherwise handled in accordance with applicable law and our operational practices.</p>

    <h2>Information Security</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO takes reasonable measures designed to protect personal information against unauthorized access, use, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.</p>
    <p>These measures may include administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards appropriate to the nature of the information and the circumstances in which it is handled.</p>
    <p>However, no website, network, electronic transmission, or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
    <p>If we become aware of a security incident involving personal information, we will respond in accordance with applicable law and our incident-response practices.</p>

    <h2>International and Cross-Border Information Handling</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO supports group travel across the United States and Canada and may work with customers, partners, and travelers located in different countries.</p>
    <p>As a result, personal information may be accessed, processed, or shared across borders where necessary to provide services or operate our business.</p>
    <p>Where applicable law requires specific safeguards, notices, consents, or contractual protections for cross-border transfers, WAYGGO will follow those requirements.</p>

    <h2>Your Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live and the laws that apply to you, you may have rights concerning your personal information.</p>
    <p>These rights may include the ability to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to personal information we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
      <li>Request deletion of certain information</li>
      <li>Request information about how your information is used or shared</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
      <li>Request a copy of certain information in a portable format</li>
      <li>Opt out of certain marketing communications</li>
      <li>Exercise other rights provided by applicable law</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Privacy rights vary by jurisdiction and are subject to legal exceptions.</p>
    <p>To exercise a privacy right, contact us using the information provided below.</p>
    <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing certain requests.</p>

    <h2>No Retaliation for Privacy Requests</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO will not knowingly discriminate against or retaliate against an individual for exercising privacy rights available to them under applicable law.</p>
    <p>Certain services or information may necessarily require certain information to be provided. Where that is the case, we will explain the relevant requirement rather than treating a privacy request as a reason to disadvantage someone.</p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO provides transportation services that may involve school groups, youth organizations, families, and other groups that include children.</p>
    <p>Our services are generally arranged by adults, organizations, schools, tour operators, travel professionals, or other responsible parties.</p>
    <p>We do not knowingly use this website to independently solicit personal information directly from children for unrelated purposes.</p>
    <p>Where information about children is provided to us for transportation purposes, we expect the organization or responsible adult providing that information to have the appropriate authority to do so.</p>
    <p>If you believe a child has provided personal information to WAYGGO improperly, please contact us.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Websites and Services</h2>
    <p>Our website or communications may contain links to third-party websites, platforms, reservation systems, social media services, or other external services.</p>
    <p>Those third parties may have their own privacy policies and practices.</p>
    <p>WAYGGO is not responsible for the privacy practices of websites or services that it does not operate.</p>
    <p>We encourage you to review the privacy information provided by third-party services before providing them with personal information.</p>

    <h2>Do Not Track and Similar Signals</h2>
    <p>Browsers and devices may provide privacy-related signals or preferences.</p>
    <p>The way these signals are recognized can vary depending on the technology and jurisdiction.</p>
    <p>Where applicable law requires WAYGGO to recognize a particular privacy signal, we will do so in accordance with that law.</p>

    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes may be necessary when:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Our services change</li>
      <li>Our website changes</li>
      <li>Our technology changes</li>
      <li>Applicable privacy laws change</li>
      <li>Our information practices change</li>
      <li>We identify opportunities to make the policy clearer</li>
    </ul>
    <p>When we update the policy, we will revise the “Last Updated” date at the top of this page.</p>
    <p>For significant changes where required by applicable law, we will provide additional notice.</p>
    <p>We encourage you to review this page periodically.</p>

    <h2>Contact WAYGGO About Privacy</h2>
    <p>If you have a question about this Privacy Policy, want to understand how your information is handled, or wish to exercise a privacy right, please contact WAYGGO.</p>
    <p><strong>WAYGGO Charters Inc.</strong></p>
    <p>You can reach our team through the <a href={withBase("/contact")}>WAYGGO contact page</a>.</p>
    <p>When submitting a privacy request, please provide enough information for us to understand your request and verify your identity where necessary.</p>
    <p>We will handle privacy requests in accordance with applicable law.</p>

    <h2>A Note About Trust</h2>
    <p>WAYGGO's business is built around coordination.</p>
    <p>Customers trust us with information about their journeys. Travel professionals trust us with client and itinerary details. Transportation partners trust us with business information.</p>
    <p>Organizations trust us to help coordinate the movement of their groups. We recognize that information is part of those relationships.</p>
    <p>Our approach is therefore simple:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Collect what we reasonably need.</li>
      <li>Use it for the purpose it was provided.</li>
      <li>Share it when necessary to deliver the service.</li>
      <li>Protect it responsibly.</li>
      <li>Be clear about our practices.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>That is how WAYGGO approaches privacy—as part of the responsibility that comes with being a transportation partner.</p>
    <p><strong>One relationship. Built on trust.</strong></p>
  </LegalContent>
</BaseLayout>
